  "@type": "Process",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Design and fabrication of the solid fuel grain for hybrid rocket engines. HTPB (hydroxyl-terminated polybutadiene) is the heritage fuel; paraffin wax delivers 3-5x higher regression rate via the entrainment of melt-layer droplets; cross-linked polymers (SHPB, dicyclopentadiene) add mechanical strength for high-thrust applications. Single-port and multi-port geometries (wagon-wheel, star) set the fuel surface area and the oxidizer-to-fuel ratio along the combustion port.",
